course: dictionary
lesson: 2471
title: Data: facts, numbers and information
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Data» is a word you will meet in maths, science and computing. In all three, it means information that has been collected so it can be studied, used or stored. Data can be numbers, words, pictures or facts.
explain: Think of a class survey. If you ask everyone how they travel to school and write down the answers, those answers are data. Once they are put into a table or a graph, the data can be studied, and you can find the mode, the mean or the range.
explain: In computing, data is the information a computer stores and sends. «Messages are turned into bits and split into packets, small chunks of data.» So when you send a message, it travels as data. Your name, address and photos are personal data, and they should be kept safe online.
fact: Data means facts, numbers or information collected so they can be studied and used.
fact: In computing, data is information stored and used by a computer.
fact: In maths and science, pupils collect data in surveys and experiments, then show it in tables, tally charts and graphs.
fact: Personal data, such as your name, address and photos, should be protected online.
fact: «Data» is usually treated as one uncountable word in everyday English, even though formally it is the plural of «datum».
exercise: «Messages are turned into bits and split into packets, small chunks of data.» What does data mean here? | *Information that a computer stores and sends | A large family of animals | Dirty water left in a bucket | A kind of dance
exercise: The class counted how many pets each child has and wrote the numbers in a table. What is the table full of? | Dragons | Dust | *Data | Dinner
exercise: «Your personal data, like your name and address, should be kept safe online.» What should be kept safe? | The router | The mobile phone battery | *Your personal information | Your favourite song
test: The scientists collected data about how many hours each child slept. What is data? | *Facts and numbers collected so they can be studied | Things you eat for lunch | A type of dance | A loud noise from a speaker
test: «In a video call the phone squeezes the video into smaller data.» Why does it do this? | To turn the video into a song | To make the video louder | To make the camera stop working | *So the video can be sent over the internet more easily
exam: «Different languages suit different jobs: Python for quick scripts, data and learning, JavaScript for websites, Rust and C++ for speed.» Which language suits data work, according to this sentence? | JavaScript | Rust | *Python | Scratch
